        "CopyrightInformation": "©2017 American Association for Cancer Research.",
        "AbstractText": "After being pulled from the market 7 years ago, gemtuzumab ozogamicin has been reapproved by the FDA, this time for adults newly diagnosed with acute myeloid leukemia, as well as patients 2 years of age and older with relapsed/refractory disease. The CD33-targeting antibody-drug conjugate can be given as a single agent or in combination with chemotherapy."
      },
